  rhythm('Sinus Bradycardia',
    'Sinus P waves precede conducted QRS complexes at a slow rate. The clinical significance depends on symptoms and perfusion, not a rate label alone.',
    'Review baseline rate, AV-nodal-slowing drugs, vagal stimuli, oxygenation and reversible causes. Significant symptomatic bradycardia requires the current resuscitation pathway.',
    'Asymptomatic baseline bradycardia does not by itself mandate cancellation or pacing. New symptomatic bradycardia requires evaluation and stabilization.',
    '$standardMonitoring Ensure rapid access to pacing when clinically indicated.',
    [bradySource, periopSource]),
  rhythm('Sinus Tachycardia',
    'Sinus P waves with an accelerated rate, usually with a consistent P-QRS relationship.',
